DASH.todo={title:"What to do as a normal investor",note:"General info, not personal financial advice.",
l:["<b>Don't react to one earnings night.</b> Alphabet's miss pulled tech futures down after hours while Microsoft rose; keep regular investing (DCA) instead of selling or buying big on today's open.",
"<b>Rates are staying high.</b> The Fed paused, but traders see an 83-90% chance of a December hike and the 10Y is above 5%; avoid new high-interest debt and lock in fixed rates where you can.",
"<b>Cash and short-term bonds still pay.</b> The 2Y is near 4.7%; short-term deposits and bonds are a fine place to wait.",
"<b>Oil risk is back up.</b> WTI is over $100 again on reported US plans for Iran strikes after the 3 Nov midterms; higher fuel can keep inflation and rate worries alive.",
"<b>Spread your risk.</b> The AI trade is splitting into winners and losers by the quarter; broad index funds beat betting on single names into earnings.",
"<b>Gold is a hedge, not a bet.</b> It is holding near $4,050; keep only a small slice.",
"<b>Keep crypto small.</b> BTC is stuck around $81k; below ~$78k support, expect more downside.",
"<b>Thai investors: hold and be selective.</b> The SET slipped 0.57% to 1,566.10 as foreigners sold ฿2.2B, and the BoT kept rates at 1.00%; KS sees support at 1,555 and 1,540 this week. In our dividend table, SPALI, TVO, PTT, ICHI and AP trade at or below their buy zones (green); check earnings and payout safety first."]};
// Glossary: m = regex matched against an element's text (li/td/h2); d = plain explanation + what it means now.
DASH.glossary={
fg:{m:"Fear & Greed",d:"CNN's 0-100 mood gauge for US stocks, built from 7 signals. 35.9 = Fear (after Wednesday's close), up from 33.6 the day before and 30.3 a week ago, as stocks rose a third day; investors are still cautious, and Alphabet's after-hours drop may weigh today."},
fgbands:{d:"0-25 Extreme Fear, 26-45 Fear, 46-55 Neutral, 56-75 Greed, 76-100 Extreme Greed. Fear often comes before rebounds, but not always."},
nk:{m:"Nuclear Escalation",d:"Our editorial 0-100 tension score from weighted news factors. Not a probability. ~45 = Elevated, up about 1 point: reports of US strike plans after the midterms and more Houthi attacks on Saudi Arabia, while Iran says diplomacy is still alive."},
nkbands:{d:"0-20 Low, 21-40 Guarded, 41-60 Elevated, 61-80 High, 81-100 Severe. Each factor's score × weight adds up to the total."},
mom:{m:"Market momentum",d:"S&P 500 vs its 125-day average. 43.4 = fear, but improving: three straight gains pulled the S&P closer to its trend."},
str:{m:"price strength",d:"Stocks at 52-week highs vs lows. 30.0 = more lows than highs, fear (48 NYSE highs vs 140 lows Wednesday)."},
brd:{m:"breadth",d:"Volume in rising vs falling stocks. 29.6 = fear: the gains are still narrow."},
pc:{m:"Put/Call",d:"Compares bets on stocks falling vs rising. 26.6 = lots of protection buying, a fearful sign."},
vix:{m:"VIX",d:"The market's 'fear gauge' of expected S&P swings. Reading 50.0 = neutral; volatility stayed calm through the Fed."},
sh:{m:"Safe-haven",d:"Stock returns vs bonds lately. 17.4 = bonds have beaten stocks, extreme fear."},
jb:{m:"Junk bond",d:"Extra yield on risky company debt. 54.0 = neutral: lenders are a little less nervous."},
f1:{m:"Active wars",d:"Wars that could pull in nuclear powers. Scored 65 (up from 62): the US reportedly told Gulf states to get ready for a short, intense Iran campaign after the midterms. Iran isn't a confirmed nuclear state."},
f2:{m:"Russia-Ukraine",d:"A nuclear power at war. Scored 37 (down from 38), the biggest weight: the Oleshky ceasefire is holding and talks are expected in early November, but strikes go on."},
f3:{m:"spillover",d:"Risk the Mideast war widens. Scored 69 (up from 68): Saudi Arabia shot down a Houthi missile aimed at Taif, and Iran says the Ras Tanura refinery's main unit is out (unconfirmed)."},
f4:{m:"diplomacy channels",d:"Are big powers talking? Higher = fewer working channels. Scored 26 (up from 24): Iran rejected Qatar's latest ideas, though it says it is still talking to mediators."},
f5:{m:"Arms-control",d:"Nuclear threats and treaty news. Scored 25 (up from 24): no explicit nuclear threats; Trump repeated that Iran must never get a nuclear weapon."},
sp:{m:"S&P",d:"500 big US companies, the main US stock benchmark. ~7,744 Wednesday (+0.28%), a third gain, but futures dipped after Alphabet's results."},
dow:{m:"Dow",d:"30 large 'blue-chip' US stocks, more old-economy. +0.19% Wednesday."},
ndq:{m:"Nasdaq",d:"Tech-heavy US index. +0.27% Wednesday; Nasdaq-100 futures fell about 1.2% after Alphabet missed, while Microsoft rose after hours."},
y10:{m:"10Y",d:"Yield on 10-year US government bonds, which drives loan rates. ~5.04% (Wednesday): back above 5% as markets bet on a December hike."},
wti:{m:"WTI",d:"US crude oil price. ~$102.8 settle Wednesday (+2.9%), back above $100 on reports of US strike plans for Iran."},
brent:{m:"Brent",d:"Global benchmark crude. ~$115.3 (December contract, +1.3% Wednesday), near a six-month high."},
dsl:{m:"diesel",d:"US average diesel price. ~$6.35/gal (AAA, 28 Oct), just under the 22 Sep record of $6.53."},
gold:{m:"^Gold$|Gold and|gold slice",d:"Classic safe haven. ~$4,059: slightly lower as higher oil and December hike bets lifted yields."},
btc:{m:"Bitcoin|BTC",d:"The largest crypto. ~$81.2k = neutral: it held around $81,000 through the Fed; ~$78k is support."},
bull:{d:"BULLISH = we expect it to rise or hold strong. MILDLY = a leaning, not a strong view."},
neu:{d:"NEUTRAL = no clear direction; it could go either way."},
bear:{d:"BEARISH = we expect it to fall or stay weak."},
ff:{m:"Fed funds",d:"The Fed's key short-term interest rate. 3.75-4.00%, held on 28 Oct with two officials wanting a hike; next decision 9 Dec."},
cpi:{m:"CPI",d:"Consumer price inflation. 3.7% YoY is well above the Fed's 2% goal."},
ppi:{m:"PPI",d:"Prices businesses pay, an early inflation signal. +6.3% in a year, the biggest since 2022."},
odds:{m:"Hike odds|Fed odds",d:"Market-implied chance of a Fed hike (fed funds futures, CME FedWatch). About 83-90% for a quarter-point hike on 9 Dec after Wednesday's hold."},
dxy:{m:"Dollar index",d:"DXY: the dollar against 6 major currencies. The dollar slipped about 0.2% Wednesday after Warsh's press conference (Reuters)."},
jpy:{m:"USD/JPY|Yen",d:"Yen per dollar. ~157.9 = a weak yen; the BOJ decides Friday 30 Oct."},
cds:{m:"CDS",d:"Credit default swap: insurance against a company defaulting. CoreWeave's CDS went past 11% (a distress level) and Meta's hit a record in October as AI spending strained cash flow."},
bot:{m:"BOT policy|BoT meeting|BOT MPC|BoT decision|BoT held|BoT kept",d:"Bank of Thailand's key rate. Held at 1.00% on 28 Oct in a unanimous vote (fourth hold in a row); the BoT sees 2026 inflation at 2.1% and is watching oil and El Niño risks."},
set:{m:"SET",d:"SET = Thai stock index; SET50 = its 50 biggest stocks. SET 1,566.10 (−0.57% Wed 28 Oct) as foreigners sold ฿2.2B; KS sees support at 1,555 and 1,540 this week."},
flow:{m:"Foreign flows|foreigners",d:"Net buying minus selling by foreign investors. −฿2.22B on 28 Oct, ending a three-day buying streak; October to date about −฿4.8B, year to date +฿20.3B (SET data)."},
dca:{m:"DCA",d:"Dollar-cost averaging: invest a fixed amount on a schedule regardless of price, which smooths out bad timing."}};
