DASH.glossary.hl={m:"Breadth",d:"New highs = NYSE stocks at a 52-week high; new lows = at a 52-week low. Index up while lows outnumber highs = a narrow bounce. Latest session (Wed 28 Oct): 48 highs vs 140 lows (WSJ) even as the S&P rose a third day. Highs ticked up from 41, but lows jumped from 108, so the rally is still narrow and chip-led. Watch whether Alphabet's slide and today's PCE push lows higher."};
