DASH.glossary.ew={d:"Early Warning Signals tracks public signs that have often come before major geopolitical events: embassy ordered/authorized departures, Level-4 travel advisories, airspace closures, and surges in military or private-jet flights. The 0-100 level is a transparent sum of these counts (see the table). It is NOT a prediction and can be noisy: headlines repeat, and official notices can lag. Use it as a reason to look closer, not to trade."};

DASH.glossary.wm={d:"World Monitor (worldmonitor.app) is a free, open-source, third-party live map that puts conflicts, military flights, ships, shipping chokepoints like Hormuz, and markets on one screen. It is useful for checking whether an Early Warning or headline claim shows up in flights or shipping. It is not our data and we do not verify it: it blocks embedding, so the button opens it in a new tab. Treat it as a second look, not a prediction."};
